{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528829-vtm-1st-edition-what-was-dust-to-dust-originally-going-to-be-like","id":1528829,"title":"(VTM 1st Edition) What was Dust To Dust originally going to be like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-18T13:26:01-08:00","id":1528829,"title":"(VTM 1st Edition) What was Dust To Dust originally going to be like?","content":"So, I've recently been on a binge of re-reading the Vampire 1st edition books I own and I'm planning to run an IRL chronicle this coming weekend with V1. It's going to be a 90's period piece with the OG Chicago By Night setting. I'm gonna start off with<i> Forged in Steel</i>, then go into<i> Ashes To Ashes</i>, and from there, incorporate a few of the scenarios in The Succubus Club and then after that, I'm not sure where to go as an ST but I've got plenty of time to figure out the post-Succubus Club parts of the game. Which brings me to the main topic of this thread.<br /> <br /> There was a lot of stuff from 1st Edition that was announced but never released or didn't get released until many years later in a very drastically altered form. Looking at the original White Wolf Magazine issue that had the pre-release packet for V1, there's references to <i>The Last Supper </i>a full four years before it came out.<br /> <br /> Probably the most famous example of a book that never was but could've been is <i>Dust To Dust</i>. It's teased in the back of <i>Ashes To Ashes</i> and I think it's also one of the books listed in the White Wolf Magazine pre-release packet. But we never got to actually see <i>Dust To Dust.</i><br /> <br /> Well, technically we did get to see it over twenty years later as one of the first V20 supplements. However, it's clear that this was not the original <i>Dust To Dust </i>but instead a farewell to the starter setting of Gary, Indiana. With stuff like zombie walks and &quot;urban necromancy&quot;, it's very much a product of the early 2010's.<br /> <br /> So when I read the V20 Dust To Dust that got published, I start to wonder what the original 1st Edition version of the supplement was going to be like? Did any of the old WW devs ever say anything about it in interviews or in online posts? Were there any fanmade attempts at trying to create the scenario? Would it have been mostly focused on Chicago instead of Gary?<br /> <br /> Part of me wonders if this &quot;V1 Dust To Dust&quot; was going to be a &quot;bridge&quot; for <i>Milwaukee By Night</i>, similar to how <i>Ashes To Ashes</i> was for <i>Chicago By Night</i> 1e (IIRC, didn't Ashes To Ashes come out a month or two before CBN 1E did?)<br /> <br /> I'm going to page <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> given he's been there from the beginning and to be honest, I think he's a cool guy and probably the most knowledgeable on VTM 1st Edition content of any of the regulars on this forum, especially when it comes to Chicago By Night and the various books connected to it.<br /> <br /> If you were going to do Dust To Dust as the 1st Edition chronicle/module it was originally intended to be, how would you go about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-18-2024, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T14:36:57-08:00","id":1528830,"title":"","content":"Hey!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the compliment.<br /> <br /> I think we can only speculate about where the plotline was originally going to go as the ASHES TO ASHES story was actually an introduction to the larger 1st Edition CHICAGO BY NIGHT. Part of the story was that the player characters would &quot;leave&quot; Gary, Indiana and it's relatively contained story of Sullivan Dane, Allicia, Evelyn Stephens, Juggler, and so on.<br /> <br /> By the time the player characters are involved in CHICAGO BY NIGHT, they are way above this sort of thing and if they've played the events of ASHES TO ASHES then they potentially have a Life Boon from Lodin (who intends to fulfill it in the most weasally evil way possible by trying to Blood Bond them).<br /> <br /> I actually can give you speculation about what DUST TO DUST was meant to be though. MILWAUKEE BY NIGHT introduced the role of Lupines into the setting and Dust to Dust was meant to close the curtain on the Chicago Chronicles. So my assumption is that the &quot;original&quot; DUST TO DUST actually is probably the predecessor to UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON.<br /> <br /> Which is that the Chronicle deals with the Death of Lodin, the introduction of Lupines (probably with more Milwaukee involvement the first time), and the introduction of the Sabbat to the majority of the players. At some point, WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE came out and they wrote a much larger role for the Lupines into the story.<br /> <br /> As we see, UABRM also transitioned Chicago from 1st Edition to 2nd Edition's Chicago by Night.<br /> <br /> While DUST TO DUST the Tournament Module is something of a disappointment, I'd like to point out it did have a very interesting &quot;end&quot; for Juggler and Modius of both of them fighting it out for dominion over a city no one wanted and Sullivan Dane learning some Kindred aren't evil (or at least are good enough to help him kill a Samedi Elder wight--a triumph of any Hunter's career prior to the Second Inquisition).<br /> <br /> I also think that Matthew Dawkins and the good folk at OPP also contributed well to updating the Gary setting with the adventure module RUSTED VEINS showing that Juggler and Modius get absolutely awful to one another. LET THE STREETS RUN RED is something I also got to contribute some of the character write-ups to as well (tweaked by professionals to be up to OPP standards). I definitely think they did a great job.<br /> <br /> I did &quot;my own&quot; DUST TO DUST actually as well called THE MURDER OF MODIUS which is a Storyteller's Vault. The premise for that is Modius is assassinated by parties unknown (Arthur Caldwell and Eric Sharpe working across sect lines) but his ghost is trying to lead the players to solve his murder--and also attempt to local Lucian's torporous form so Modius can diablerize him while possessing a Thin Blood medium.<br /> <br /> (And several other parties want to do the same)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T15:51:50-08:00","id":1528836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528829-vtm-1st-edition-what-was-dust-to-dust-originally-going-to-be-like?p=1528830#post1528830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the compliment.<br /> <br /> I think we can only speculate about where the plotline was originally going to go as the ASHES TO ASHES story was actually an introduction to the larger 1st Edition CHICAGO BY NIGHT. Part of the story was that the player characters would &quot;leave&quot; Gary, Indiana and it's relatively contained story of Sullivan Dane, Allicia, Evelyn Stephens, Juggler, and so on.<br /> <br /> By the time the player characters are involved in CHICAGO BY NIGHT, they are way above this sort of thing and if they've played the events of ASHES TO ASHES then they potentially have a Life Boon from Lodin (who intends to fulfill it in the most weasally evil way possible by trying to Blood Bond them).<br /> <br /> I actually can give you speculation about what DUST TO DUST was meant to be though. MILWAUKEE BY NIGHT introduced the role of Lupines into the setting and Dust to Dust was meant to close the curtain on the Chicago Chronicles. So my assumption is that the &quot;original&quot; DUST TO DUST actually is probably the predecessor to UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON.<br /> <br /> Which is that the Chronicle deals with the Death of Lodin, the introduction of Lupines (probably with more Milwaukee involvement the first time), and the introduction of the Sabbat to the majority of the players. At some point, WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE came out and they wrote a much larger role for the Lupines into the story.<br /> <br /> As we see, UABRM also transitioned Chicago from 1st Edition to 2nd Edition's Chicago by Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really a fan of any of the V5 stuff in general, but I do like the idea that Dust To Dust was probably going to be tied to both Lupines and Milwaukee By Night. Milwaukee By Night involves the Lupines in the setting and I could see this 1e version of Dust To Dust being either the &quot;bridge&quot; to Milwaukee By Night or the &quot;bridge&quot; to a pre-WTA version of <i>Under A Blood Red Moon.</i><br /> <br /> Maybe I should write up a Lupine-focused Dust To Dust for my upcoming CbN chronicle. It'll be a while though since there will be a lot of stuff to do. After the Forged In Steel and Ashes To Ashes 